# PCE1 Workspace Rules
- Project root contains KiCad files (`Ge_Parametric_Engine.kicad_*`), `firmware/`, `webapp/`, `android_app/`, `artifacts/`, and `handoff/`.
- Check `handoff/` and `artifacts/` (and `agent_state/` if present) first to establish current phase and gate status.
- Read only the single file required for the active task; never bulk-load the repo into context.
- Update the relevant markdown state/audit file in `artifacts/` whenever a design change or gate check completes.
- Use `ge-swarm` MCP tools (`ask_mac_node`, `run_swarm_agent`) for heavy math verification, scouting, or parallel subtasks.

## Autonomous Execution Rules
- Never stop mid-file when read_file truncates output. Immediately read the remaining line ranges (e.g. 714-1467) until you have inspected the full file.
- Never end a turn with a menu of options ("Would you like me to 1/2/3") while tasks remain. Execute the full task, run verification commands, and only call attempt_completion after all changes are tested and verified.
- Local macOS KiCad libraries (if installed): /Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/SharedSupport/symbols and /Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/SharedSupport/footprints. Check those paths before claiming KiCad libraries are inaccessible.

